text: ['({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a Goblin.\\nGoblin Grenade deals 5 damage to any target.', 'Battle cry (Whenever this creature attacks, each other attacking creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.)', 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Create a 5/5 blue Wall creature token with defender. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Create three 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', 'Create two 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', 'Creatures you control gain double strike until end of turn. (They deal both first-strike and regular combat damage.)', 'Cycling {1}{R} ({1}{R}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Gempalm Incinerator, you may have it deal X damage to target creature, where X is the number of Goblins on the battlefield.', 'Double strike\\nWhenever Warren Instigator deals damage to an opponent, you may put a Goblin creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', 'Draw X cards.', 'Draw three cards.', "Enchant creature\\nWhen Claustrophobia enters the battlefield, tap enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", "Flying\\nBattle Squadron's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures you control.", 'Flying\\nWhen Merfolk Wayfinder enters the battlefield, reveal the top three cards of your library. Put all Island cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Forgotten Cave enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}.\\nCycling {R} ({R}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Ghostfire is colorless.\\nGhostfire deals 3 damage to any target.', "Goblin Goon can't attack unless you control more creatures than defending player.\\nGoblin Goon can't block unless you control more creatures than attacking player.", 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nOther Goblin creatures you control get +1/+1 and have haste.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nWhen Goblin Ringleader enters the battlefield, reveal the top four cards of your library. Put all Goblin cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nWhen Inkfathom Divers enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library, then put them back in any order.", "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nWhenever Cold-Eyed Selkie deals combat damage to a player, you may draw that many cards.", 'Lonely Sandbar enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}.\\nCycling {U} ({U}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Menace (This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", 'Other Goblin creatures you control attack each combat if able.\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, create a 1/1 red Goblin creature token with haste.\\nWhenever Goblin Rabblemaster attacks, it gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each other attacking Goblin.', "Other Merfolk creatures you control get +1/+1 and have islandwalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Other Merfolk creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever you cast a Merfolk spell, you may tap or untap target permanent.', "Other Merfolk creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{T}: Target Merfolk creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'Protection from red\\nElemental creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhen Master of Waves enters the battlefield, create a number of 1/0 blue Elemental creature tokens equal to your devotion to blue. (Each {U} in the mana costs of permanents you control counts toward your devotion to blue.)', 'Put a flood counter on target land. That land is an Island in addition to its other types for as long as it has a flood counter on it. If you control a Merfolk, draw a card.', "Renown 1 (When this creature deals combat damage to a player, if it isn't renowned, put a +1/+1 counter on it and it becomes renowned.)\\nAs long as Goblin Glory Chaser is renowned, it has menace. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", "Return to their owners' hands all creatures with toughness less than or equal to the number of Islands you control.", 'Tarfire deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Target creature gets +3/+1 and gains trample until end of turn.', 'Untap all creatures that attacked this turn. After this main phase, there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase.', "Up to two target creatures each get +0/+3 until end of turn. Untap those creatures. At this turn's next end of combat, tap each creature that was blocked by one of those creatures this turn and it doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'When Tidal Courier enters the battlefield, reveal the top four cards of your library. Put all Merfolk cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\n{3}{U}: Tidal Courier gains flying until end of turn.', "When Tidebinder Mage enters the battlefield, tap target red or green creature an opponent controls. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as you control Tidebinder Mage.", 'Whenever Scroll Thief deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.', 'Whenever a permanent you control becomes untapped, Wake Thrasher gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever another red creature enters the battlefield under your control, Foundry Street Denizen gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "You may cast Harbinger of the Tides as though it had flash if you pay {2} more to cast it. (You may cast it any time you could cast an instant.)\\nWhen Harbinger of the Tides enters the battlefield, you may return target tapped creature an opponent controls to its owner's hand.", "You may exile a blue card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nChange the target of target spell with a single target.", '{1}, Sacrifice Ember Hauler: It deals 2 damage to any target.', '{1}{R}, Sacrifice a land: Put a +1/+1 counter on Goblin Razerunners.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, you may have Goblin Razerunners deal damage equal to the number of +1/+1 counters on it to target player or planeswalker.', '{3}, {T}: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a land card. Goblin Charbelcher deals damage equal to the number of nonland cards revealed this way to any target. If the revealed land card was a Mountain, Goblin Charbelcher deals double that damage instead. Put the revealed cards on the bottom of your library in any order.', '{4}, {T}, Exile Brittle Effigy: Exile target creature.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Blighted Gorge: It deals 2 damage to any target.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{5}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice Blighted Cataract: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Create X 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens, where X is the number of Goblins you control.', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Each creature attacks this turn if able.', '{T}: Rootwater Hunter deals 1 damage to any target.', "{T}: Target Merfolk creature gets +1/+1 and gains islandwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\n{T}: Target land becomes an Island until end of turn.", "{T}: Target creature with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Target land becomes an Island until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"A true warrior fights with whatever\'s handy."\\n—Qerk of the Secret Warren', '"After Auntie brushed the soot from her eyes, she discovered something wonderful: the fire had turned the goat into something that smelled delicious."\\n—A tale of Auntie Grub', '"Be like the sea: flow around that which is unmovable; for everything else, crash into it unrelentingly."', '"Bitter water, vicious wave;\\nShadow-cold shallows, root-made maze.\\nHome\'s angry embrace."\\n—*Rootwater Saga*', '"He displays a perverse charisma fueled by avarice. Highly dangerous. Recommend civil sanctions."\\n—Agmand Sarv, Azorius hussar', '"In my early experiments in phylactery, I found that fragile forms have their uses."\\n—Rocati, Duke of Martyne', '"It\'s time for the \'Smash, Smash\' song!"', '"Leave no scraps, lest you attract pests."\\n—Mardu threat', '"Let the land dwellers know the coast is no longer the border between our realms. A new age of empire has begun."', '"The best way over the mountain is through."', '"The floor of the sea is paved with the shattered remnants of vessels that navigated its surface unwelcomed."\\n—Thassa, god of the sea', '"The tides have begun to ignore the moon."\\n—Tamiyo\'s journal', '"The treasure in my mind is greater than any worldly glory."', '"What you attempt to pull from the aether, I can spread onto the wind."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"You may want to hold your breath."\\n—Kellyg, merrow aquitect', 'After the Foundry Street riot, Arrester Hulbein tried to ban bludgeons. Which, inevitably, resulted in another riot.', 'Anyone who thinks merrows have more brains than brawn has never been run over by one.', "Don't underestimate the aerodynamic qualities of the common goblin.", 'Finding themselves in a new and unexplored world, they immediately set it on fire.', 'Flurk\'s crude goblin language didn\'t differentiate between "I *bring* the flame" and "I *am* the flame."', 'Fragments of thought refract and multiply, surging in a geyser of dizzying insight.', 'Goblins are eager to follow orders, especially when those orders involve stealing, hurting, annoying, eating, destroying, or swearing.', "He has the biggest bashing stick, so it's a safe bet he's the leader.", "It's not the size of the rock. It's how badly you want to lift it.", 'Kapsho merfolk have infiltrated fortresses as remote as the desert citadel in Sunari in their relentless quest for arcane knowledge.', 'Measure once, cut twice.', "Merfolk don't always know what they're looking for, but they're certain once they find it.", 'Once, water ran here. Now only dust and ash fall from the clifftops.', 'Only those gifted with the eye of Ugin, the spirit dragon, can see his fiery breath.', 'She follows the old tributaries built when merrows still shaped the tides.', 'Six feet of earth muffled his cries.', 'Steady and silent as the deep current, the reejerey guides the course of the school.', 'The goblins made an unruly pile with military precision.', 'The land is dying, but it will not go peacefully.', 'The tide of battle favors those who can swim.', 'There is always a rabble to be roused.', 'When you need to convey that special kind of message.']
artist: ['Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Austin Hsu', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Brom', 'Chippy', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Daren Bader', 'Dave Kendall', 'Dimitar Marinski', 'Gabor Szikszai', 'Greg Staples', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'Jon Foster', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Mark Behm', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Noah Bradley', 'Omar Rayyan', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Sam Wood', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Vincent Proce', 'Wayne Reynolds', "William O'Connor", 'Zoltan Boros', 'rk post']
